    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into favorable matchups against vulnerable starters. The strongest play on the board is **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), who benefits from a potent combination of a high-ceiling park factor (+14%) and a soft matchup against Nick Martinez. He is closely followed by **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03), who is our premier weapon against the Lauer start, leveraging an elite SP skill boost (+19%) and a favorable batting order position (#2). **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) also warrants attention; despite the general caution regarding Rhett Lowder, **Soderstrom** captures a strong SP skill bonus, making him a cornerstone in our push for power and RBI. **Corbin Carroll** remains a mandatory start due to his stolen base profile, and while his score (67.66) is slightly dampened by the threat of Mize, his upside in a #1 hole remains the anchor of our speed-starved category goals.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins was the exclusion of **Cole Young** (36.38). While **Young** projects well in terms of plate appearances at the top of his order, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to **Travis Bazzana** (44.93) due to the latter\u2019s superior platoon leverage (+7%) against Christian Scott. We are also monitoring **Austin Riley** (51.86) closely; he is currently active in the UTIL slot, but he carries a 33% rain risk that could compromise his impact. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Josh Naylor** (47.00) and **Brice Turang** (50.30); both face the significant hurdle of elite arm talent in Drew Anderson and Paul Skenes, respectively. While their raw projections remain above our floor, we are prepared to pivot if the \"Lineup Pending\" status confirms any unfavorable shifts that further erode their efficiency against these high-strikeout hurlers.",
